1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Excuse me, officer.

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,478
Can you help me?

3
00:00:03,478 --> 00:00:03,728
Sure.

4
00:00:03,728 --> 00:00:05,222
Can you tell me

5
00:00:05,222 --> 00:00:06,916
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

6
00:00:06,916 --> 00:00:08,356
Riverdale, New York."

7
00:00:08,356 --> 00:00:10,934
You should take the number 1 subway.

8
00:00:10,934 --> 00:00:12,845
Is there a station near here?

9
00:00:12,845 --> 00:00:14,890
Yes. The station's that way.

10
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,008
You should take the number 1 train

11
00:00:18,008 --> 00:00:18,208
to Van Cortlandt Park.

12
00:00:18,008 --> 00:00:20,582
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

13
00:00:20,582 --> 00:00:21,846
Anytime. Good luck.

14
00:00:21,846 --> 00:00:26,491
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

15
00:00:26,491 --> 00:00:26,802
Thank you.

16
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:44,669
You're welcome.

17
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,647
Is this pink too bright for me?

18
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:56,581
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

19
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:02,537
Try this. It's size eight.

20
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:04,537
But I wear size ten.

21
00:01:04,537 --> 00:01:09,243
How about green? It's size ten.

22
00:01:09,243 --> 00:01:11,471
Let me try it on.

23
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:17,427
I'm taking too much of your time.

24
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:19,907
It's six o'clock.

25
00:01:19,907 --> 00:01:20,405
Where's my husband?

26
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:23,607
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

27
00:01:23,607 --> 00:01:26,123
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

28
00:01:26,123 --> 00:01:29,339
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

29
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,859
I'll take this green sweater.

30
00:01:30,859 --> 00:01:33,313
I like the color on me, don't you?

31
00:01:33,313 --> 00:01:41,251
I think it looks terrific on you.

32
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:42,362
I'm sorry I'm so late.

33
00:01:42,362 --> 00:01:45,082
I had a really bad day.

34
00:01:45,082 --> 00:01:47,207
It's ten after six. We're late.

35
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,127
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

36
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:52,185
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

37
00:01:52,185 --> 00:01:53,903
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

38
00:01:53,903 --> 00:01:56,546
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

39
00:01:56,546 --> 00:01:58,980
I lost a whole day's work.

40
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:01,798
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

41
00:02:01,798 --> 00:02:08,052
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

42
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,330
Hello.

43
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:12,530
Yes. The number, please,

44
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:18,906
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

45
00:02:18,906 --> 00:02:22,942
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

46
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
Thank you.

47
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,898
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

48
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:29,391
Hello.

49
00:02:29,391 --> 00:02:33,590
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

50
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:35,854
a small canvas bag,

51
00:02:35,854 --> 00:02:43,788
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

52
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,288
Maybe someone will find it.

53
00:02:46,288 --> 00:02:47,116
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

54
00:02:47,116 --> 00:02:51,184
And the telephone number is five five five...

55
00:02:51,184 --> 00:02:58,678
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

56
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

57
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:05,364
Thanks, anyway.

58
00:03:05,364 --> 00:03:08,412
There was a girl on the ferry.

59
00:03:08,412 --> 00:03:09,012
Now maybe...

60
00:03:09,012 --> 00:03:10,612
Tell me about it on the way home.
